{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 49, :comments ["<b>As the eagle swoops.</b> This is Vespasian and Titus, who were kings of the kings of Edom, and they destroyed the Second Temple. And thus did the Rabbis, of blessed memory, expound concerning Vespasian: he expected to come in ten days but came in five, and he heard children saying ישא ה' עליך גוי מרחוק מקצה הארץ כאשר ידאה הנשר — and he said: perhaps I am that eagle. And all these reproofs befell in the Second Temple, and there all of them were fulfilled."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:51:42.729509105Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}